  "salt": "KmOJGmOvOhF2ygrPUI7Mwg==",
  "text": "Merry Maidens is the name of several stone circles in Britain. A local legend says the stones were once women. They danced on a Sunday and so were turned into rock. Some circles are called the 'nine maidens.' That name may come from 'noon,' the ninth hour of the church day. At one site, couples danced all night. A dark man took the violin and played a tune. All the dancers became stone at the break of day. The tale is told in many regions, from Cumbria to the Shetland Isles. In Cumbria, the circle Long Meg and her Daughters carries the same story.",
  "objective": "Document the Merry Maidens, the British stone circles with a dancing legend.",
